From f8982844971fe4f413fc601a5533f099f18abb9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(core): retain decode-frontier SWA checkpoints and order
 hybrid KV eviction tail-to-root

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 2756478b60b90700b9918b457aeb38657da637b5.

Rationale:
Multi-turn 64K-100K agent conversations with hybrid FullAttention (block_size=256) + SlidingWindow (block_size=128, window=128) KV cache and sparse prefix_cache_retention_interval (512 on tp3-triangle, 8192 on tp4-ring) lose prefix-cache hits across decode boundaries and under shared BlockPool eviction pressure due to three gaps in vllm/v1/core/:
1. Decode-frontier SWA checkpoint loss: SparseRetentionPolicy._retain only retained segment multiples (k * interval) and prompt boundaries (request.num_prompt_tokens). During decode (num_tokens > request.num_prompt_tokens), whenever a turn stopped at T_end with T_end % 256 >= 128 on a non-segment boundary, SlidingWindowManager.remove_skipped_blocks freed the 128-token SWA block at floor(T_end / 256) * 256 un-hashed before free() ran, causing the next turn to miss the decoded 256-token boundary.
2. Hybrid KV eviction under shared BlockPool pressure: KVCacheCoordinator.free released all FullAttentionManager blocks before SlidingWindowManager blocks (group-major), while SlidingWindowManager.remove_skipped_blocks freed skipped SWA checkpoints in ascending token order across steps and left even a turn's own endpoint SWA checkpoint (when T_end % 256 >= 128) and all fallback SWA checkpoints unanchored at the LRU head. Under moderate eviction pressure, evicting all SWA checkpoints ahead of live MLA blocks collapsed prefix hits to 0 with all MLA blocks still cached; conversely, pulling every interior SWA checkpoint behind live MLA blocks forced light eviction to shave active conversation tops.
3. Un-cached boundary crossing on speculative decode stopping steps: Scheduler._update_request_with_output omitted kv_cache_manager.cache_blocks when a running request crossed a block boundary via accepted draft tokens on the same step that stopped the request, and AsyncScheduler._update_request_with_output lacked a staleness and num_tokens clamp guard.

Fix all three gaps:
- In SlidingWindowManager.cache_blocks, retain the active decode frontier (resend_lo, resend_hi, aligned_ext) SWA tail blocks across 256-token MLA boundaries while recycling obsolete intermediate non-segment decode-frontier SWA blocks (un-hashing and prepending to the scratch front of free_block_queue via prepend_n), leaving only the final turn endpoint SWA checkpoint cached at turn completion alongside sparse segment checkpoints.
- Track per-request retained SWA checkpoints (_req_retained_blocks) and prefix-chain inheritance (_block_prefix_chain) in SlidingWindowManager, and organize KVCacheCoordinator.free and pop_blocks_for_free into a two-tier tail-to-root order:
  * Tier 0 (aged SWA head, right after unhashed free blocks): non-anchored interior/superseded SWA blocks ordered descending by end_token (0 within-tier inversions), absorbing light pool pressure without evicting live top MLA blocks.
  * Tier 1 (active conversation tail-to-root run at MRU tail): all full-attention blocks paired with the active turn-endpoint SWA checkpoint (max_full_end) and a sparse fallback SWA checkpoint ladder (root + highest checkpoint <= max_full_end - 1024, plus 4096-token multiples when > 32 checkpoints exist) ordered by (-end_token, is_sparse, group_id, -blk_idx) (0 within-tier inversions), so deeper eviction steps down cleanly to retained checkpoints without collapsing hits to 0.
- In Scheduler._update_request_with_output and AsyncScheduler._update_request_with_output, call kv_cache_manager.cache_blocks(request, min(request.num_computed_tokens, request.num_tokens)) whenever a non-stale running request advances num_computed_tokens with zero remaining output placeholders before freeing on stop.

Quality:
Bit- and mathematically identical KV attention and compressor contents; preserves decoded frontier and shared prefix checkpoints across turns and under both light and deep LRU eviction.

Tests:
- pytest --noconftest tests/v1/core/test_prefix_cache_retention_probe.py tests/v1/core/test_prefix_caching.py and 21 sibling v1 core/scheduler test files (2681 passed across 2 fresh container boots on sp8).

Upstream status: local fix for hybrid MLA + SWA sparse prefix-cache retention and two-tier checkpoint-floor eviction ordering.
